From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:16:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 35/36] moe cache: KV segment phase 2 -- review fixes (source
 counters, idle hint)

Three small fixes from the logic review of the two phase 2 commits.  None
changes which bytes are read.

- The KV-copy candidate of a small prefill ubatch is now looked up
  whether or not GGML_MOE_KV_SEG_PF is set (still only with the KV
  segment on), and only its use is gated on the switch.  With the switch
  off the expert is read from the RAM tier / file exactly as before but
  counted under "with a KV copy", so the off-state report sizes what the
  switch would move, as the previous commit message said it did.

- The by-source counters count each staged expert once.  The callers
  collect them locally and add them only when the fill is accepted, so
  an in-place prepare that declines after building its list and falls
  through to the plain routed fill is no longer counted twice, and the
  in-place and pad entries of the in-place prepare, which that fill does
  not copy, are no longer counted as arena reads.

- The server sends llama_kv_lend_hint(0) on the all-idle return of
  update_slots, so the floor of a finished or cancelled prompt does not
  outlive it until the next request; the comment at the hint now says
  what is sent and when.
